<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Template for `xcodebuild -exportArchive` in the iOS/iPadOS DEVICE flow (Scripts/package.sh
  --ios-device), an .ipa you can install on your own iPhone or iPad. __TEAM_ID__ is substituted
  from signing.local.sh into a copy under build/ at run time, so no team id is committed.

  method=debugging is the whole difference from the App Store template beside it. The name is
  Xcode's for the DISTRIBUTION CHANNEL, not the build configuration: it is the current spelling of
  what used to be "development", which Xcode 26 still accepts while warning that it is deprecated.
  Nothing about it makes this a Debug build.

  The archive is the SAME Release configuration: optimized, no debug scaffolding. What changes is
  who the export is signed for. This profile embeds the team's REGISTERED DEVICES, which is exactly
  what makes the result installable; an app-store-connect export carries no device list and iOS
  refuses to launch it, which is why that .ipa cannot be sideloaded and this one can.

  What it costs, and it is worth saying plainly: development signing brings development
  entitlements. `aps-environment` is `development`, so push tokens are sandbox tokens, anything
  exercising real APNs delivery needs the TestFlight build, not this one. Everything that is a
  property of the compiled code, optimization, timing, memory, R8-equivalent stripping, is
  identical to what ships.

  destination=export writes a local .ipa rather than uploading. manageAppVersionAndBuildNumber=false
  is LOAD-BEARING for the same reason as the App Store template: the CFBundleVersion is the dotted
  UTC timestamp package.sh stamps (docs/versioning.md), and letting Xcode "manage" it would clobber
  that stamp, so a device build reports the same version a store build would.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>method</key>
    <string>debugging</string>
    <key>teamID</key>
    <string>__TEAM_ID__</string>
    <key>signingStyle</key>
    <string>automatic</string>
    <key>destination</key>
    <string>export</string>
    <key>manageAppVersionAndBuildNumber</key>
    <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
